From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:16:42 +0800
Subject: core/shell: experimental.no_shell_background removes the model's
 background option

With the flag on, the shell tool's input schema and description sent to the
model drop the background option (read per request in the context hook, so a
config change applies to the next request), and a background request runs in
the foreground. The user can still move a running command to the background;
the result then says the user did it, asks the model not to wait or poll, and
the completion still arrives as a steer. Off by default (upstream behavior).

Ocelot-Patch: core/no-shell-background

